    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0607" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/3–1844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Near Eastern
                        and African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-18">March 18, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Stettinius</hi>: I think you would wish to know
                    that after the meeting of your group<anchor n="80" xml:id="d649-f1"/> yesterday
                    in the Secretary’s office, Dr. Bowman<anchor n="81" xml:id="d649-f2"/> and I had
                    a moment to discuss with the Secretary the attached draft text of a joint
                    American-British statement on Palestine.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d649-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>As you will recall, you sent the President the substance of such a statement
                    during the Secretary’s absence<anchor n="83" xml:id="d649-f4"/> and the
                    President approved of issuing it after consultation with the British.</p>
                <pb facs="0608" n="596" xml:id="pg596"/>
                <p>During our conversation with the Secretary yesterday on this subject he expressed
                    general approval of the attached form of the statement but suggested that we
                    might hold it for discussion with the British when we get to London.</p>
                <p>I think this procedure is a good one, particularly for the purpose of avoiding
                    leaks that are almost inevitable if we start exchanging telegrams with London on
                    this subject. Meanwhile, however, the Secretary said he wished to clear the
                    draft statement in its present form with the President at an early moment, and I
                    have left a copy with him for that purpose.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
